.env
.env.local

# Nested env files too. The root .env is the single source of truth and `apps/web/next.config.ts`
# loads its NEXT_PUBLIC_ values, so a per-app copy should never be needed. These patterns exist
# because "should never be needed" is not the same as "cannot happen", and the cost of being wrong
# once is a published private key.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
.runtime/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
.next/
.DS_Store
broadcast/*/dry-run/

